<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97332" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρωμᾰτ-εύς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">έως</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>coverlet, bedspread</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				38
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				115
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				4.2.7
			</span></i>; also,= <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρωματόδεσμον</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				7.79
			</span></i>, condemned in this sense by <i><span class="en">
				Phryn.
				379
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in pl.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρωματεῖς</span>, <i>patchwork</i>,
			as title of literary <u>Miscellanies</u>, <i><span class="en">
				Gell.
				<u>Praef.</u>
				7
			</span></i>; the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρωματεῖς</span> of <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
			</span></i> is cited by <i><span class="en">
				Eus.
				<u>PE</u>
				1.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a flat fish marked with divers colours</i>, Philo ap.<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				7.322a
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
